uestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"As early as the seventeenth century, ergot, the fungus of rye, was used to facilitate childbirth.","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"As early as the seventeenth century, ergot, the fungus of rye, was used to facilitate childbirth.","DataExportTag":"Q331","QuestionID":"QID331"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID162","SecondaryAttribute":"As food supplies began to run low, and as the colonists faced hunger and disease, they saw that t...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"As food supplies began to run low, and as the colonists faced hunger and disease, they saw that they needed to work together if the colony was to survive.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q162","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"As food supplies began to run low, and as the colonists faced hunger and disease, they saw that t...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID162"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID352","SecondaryAttribute":"As food supplies began to run low, and as the colonists faced hunger and disease, they saw that t...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"As food supplies began to run low, and as the colonists faced hunger and disease, they saw that they needed to work together if the colony was to survive.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"As food supplies began to run low, and as the colonists faced hunger and disease, they saw that t...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"As food supplies began to run low, and as the colonists faced hunger and disease, they saw that they needed to work together if the colony was to survive.","DataExportTag":"Q352","QuestionID":"QID352"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID160","SecondaryAttribute":"At first, the settlers at Jamestown had to shepherd themselves.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"At first, the settlers at Jamestown had to shepherd themselves.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q160","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"At first, the settlers at Jamestown had to shepherd themselves.","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID160"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID350","SecondaryAttribute":"At first, the settlers had to look out for themselves. ","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"At first, the settlers had to look out for themselves.&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"At first, the settlers had to look out for themselves. ","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"At first, the settlers at Jamestown had to shepherd themselves.","DataExportTag":"Q350","QuestionID":"QID350","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID290","SecondaryAttribute":"Atomic energy is the energy that holds the nucleus of an atom together.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Atomic energy is the energy that holds the nucleus of an atom together.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Atomic energy is the energy that holds the nucleus of an atom together.","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"The nucleus of an atom is held together by a kind of energy called atomic energy.","DataExportTag":"Q290","QuestionID":"QID290","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID291","SecondaryAttribute":"Atomic reactions in which nuclei of helium are built up from nuclei of hydrogen are believed to b...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Atomic reactions in which nuclei of helium are built up from nuclei of hydrogen are believed to be the origin of the sun\u2019s energy.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Atomic reactions in which nuclei of helium are built up from nuclei of hydrogen are believed to b...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"The sun\u2019s energy comes from atomic reactions.","DataExportTag":"Q291","QuestionID":"QID291","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID45","SecondaryAttribute":"But a strain of dark dread began to creep through this happy life.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"But a strain of dark dread began to creep through this happy life.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q45","QuestionID":"QID45","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"But a strain of dark dread began to creep through this happy life.","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":1,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID371","SecondaryAttribute":"But after his death, El Greco was forgotten by history for nearly three hundred years, until he w...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"But after his death, El Greco was forgotten by history for nearly three hundred years, until he was rediscovered by artists and critics of the twentieth century.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"But after his death, El Greco was forgotten by history for nearly three hundred years, until he w...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"He prospered there for the rest of his life.","DataExportTag":"Q371","QuestionID":"QID371","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID108","SecondaryAttribute":"But it was a comedown in the mid-1960\u2019s when scientists involved in the Mars exploration studied..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"But it was a comedown in the mid-1960\u2019s when scientists involved in the Mars exploration studied photographs taken by some of the early Mariner space flights.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q108","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"But it was a comedown in the mid-1960\u2019s when scientists involved in the Mars exploration studied...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID108"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID120","SecondaryAttribute":"But still, public enthusiasm for Martian exploration wilted.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"But still, public enthusiasm for Martian exploration wilted.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q120","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"But still, public enthusiasm for Martian exploration wilted.","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID120"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID318","SecondaryAttribute":"But still, public enthusiasm for Martian exploration wilted.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"But still, public enthusiasm for Martian exploration wilted.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"But still, public enthusiasm for Martian exploration wilted.","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"But still, public enthusiasm for Martian exploration wilted.","DataExportTag":"Q318","QuestionID":"QID318"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID261","SecondaryAttribute":"But through this happy life a strain of dark foreboding began to creep. ","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"But through this happy life a strain of dark foreboding began to creep.&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"But through this happy life a strain of dark foreboding began to creep. ","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":1,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"But a strain of dark dread began to creep through this happy life.","DataExportTag":"Q261","QuestionID":"QID261","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID391","SecondaryAttribute":"But, the factors that make people four-pack-a-day smokers must surely make them different from ty...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"But, the factors that make people four-pack-a-day smokers must surely make them different from typical nonsmokers in other ways.&nbsp;&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"But, the factors that make people four-pack-a-day smokers must surely make them different from ty...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Whatever the factors are that contribute to a person\u2019s being a heavy smoker surely must also make him different from the typical nonsmoker in other ways.","DataExportTag":"Q391","QuestionID":"QID391","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID206","SecondaryAttribute":"By contrast with experimental designs, subjects, in correlational designs, in a sense, assign the...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"By contrast with experimental designs, subjects, in correlational designs, in a sense, assign themselves to conditions.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q206","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"By contrast with experimental designs, subjects, in correlational designs, in a sense, assign the...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID206"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID205","SecondaryAttribute":"By the influence on the results of some extraneous variable that is tied to or correlated with th...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"By the influence on the results of some extraneous variable that is tied to or correlated with the variable under investigation is insured against.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q205","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"By the influence on the results of some extraneous variable that is tied to or correlated with th...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID205"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID122","SecondaryAttribute":"By the time Viking I touched down on the Plain of Chryse in August, few seemed to care at all. ","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"By the time Viking I touched down on the Plain of Chryse in August, few seemed to care at all.&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q122","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"By the time Viking I touched down on the Plain of Chryse in August, few seemed to care at all. ","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID122"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID195","SecondaryAttribute":"By using stark contrasts of light and shadow, Caravaggio managed to conjure up unforgettable scen...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"By using stark contrasts of light and shadow, Caravaggio managed to conjure up unforgettable scenes of dramatic realism.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q195","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"By using stark contrasts of light and shadow, Caravaggio managed to conjure up unforgettable scen...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID195"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID382","SecondaryAttribute":"By using stark contrasts of light and shadow, Caravaggio managed to conjure up unforgettable scen...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"By using stark contrasts of light and shadow, Caravaggio managed to conjure up unforgettable scenes of dramatic realism.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"By using stark contrasts of light and shadow, Caravaggio managed to conjure up unforgettable scen...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"By using stark contrasts of light and shadow, Caravaggio managed to conjure up unforgettable scenes of dramatic realism.","DataExportTag":"Q382","QuestionID":"QID382"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID165","SecondaryAttribute":"Captain John Smith was chosen as president of the council to see that the laws were implemented. ","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Captain John Smith was chosen as president of the council to see that the laws were implemented.&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q165","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Captain John Smith was chosen as president of the council to see that the laws were implemented. ","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID165"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID381","SecondaryAttribute":"Caravaggio\u2019s critics complained that he treated exalted religious subjects in a low, vulgar style.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Caravaggio\u2019s critics complained that he treated exalted religious subjects in a low, vulgar style, because he included in his paintings the faces and figures from the street of common people.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Caravaggio\u2019s critics complained that he treated exalted religious subjects in a low, vulgar style...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Caravaggio\u2019s critics complained that he treated sacred religious subjects in a low, vulgar way by including the faces and figures of common people in his paintings.","DataExportTag":"Q381","QuestionID":"QID381","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID194","SecondaryAttribute":"Caravaggio\u2019s critics complained that he treated sacred religious subjects in a low, vulgar way by.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Caravaggio\u2019s critics complained that he treated sacred religious subjects in a low, vulgar way by including the faces and figures of common people in his paintings.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q194","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Caravaggio\u2019s critics complained that he treated sacred religious subjects in a low, vulgar way by...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID194"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1","SecondaryAttribute":"Click to write the question text","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Click to write the question text","DataExportTag":"Q1","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Click to write the question text","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Take the Survey"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":2,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID1","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID679","SecondaryAttribute":"Click to write the question text","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Click to write the question text","DataExportTag":"Q654","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Click to write the question text","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Click to write Choice 1"},"2":{"Display":"Click to write Choice 2"},"3":{"Display":"Click to write Choice 3"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID679"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID764","SecondaryAttribute":"Click to write the question text","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Click to write the question text","DataExportTag":"Q739","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Click to write the question text","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Click to write Choice 1"},"2":{"Display":"Click to write Choice 2"},"3":{"Display":"Click to write Choice 3"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID764"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID766","SecondaryAttribute":"Consent to Participate in a Research Study Pacific Lutheran University Title of Study: The effect...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div><strong>Consent to Participate in a Research Study<br \/>\nPacific Lutheran University<\/strong><\/div>\n\n<div><br \/>\n<strong>Title of Study:<\/strong> The effect of mind wandering and text difficulty on reading comprehension: A replication study.&nbsp;<br \/>\n<strong>Investigators: <\/strong>&nbsp;Alexis Herion and Cammy Widman, senior undergraduate students&nbsp;<br \/>\n<strong>Introduction<\/strong><\/div>\n<u>You are being asked to be in a research study conducted at Pacific Lutheran University in Psychology. You were selected to participate because you are at least 18 years old AND:&nbsp; <u> You are a PLU student with a SONA-systems account OR You were recruited via social media The purpose of the study is to see the effect mind wandering and text difficulty has on reading comprehension. The purpose of this is to try to see the level of cognitive difficulty that results in more mind wandering. Also, to see if interest level affects mind wandering and reading comprehension. <\/u><\/u>\n\n<div><u><u><strong>Description of the Study Procedures<\/strong><\/u><\/u><\/div>\n<u><u> <u> If you agree to be in this study, you will be asked to do the following things: Take a reading comprehension test on a computer or smartphone, which consists of eight passages for you to read and answer the corresponding questions at the end of each passage. As you read, you will be interrupted periodically with a question that asks if you were mind wandering while you read the previous sentence.&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;MS Mincho&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">After you finish reading all the passages and answering the corresponding reading comprehension questions, you will rate how interested you were in each passage that you previously read.<\/span>After you finish reading each passage and answering the corresponding reading comprehension questions, you will rate &nbsp;how interested you were in the passage you previously read. The test should take you about 15 to 30 minutes.&nbsp; Some sample questions we will ask are: &ldquo;The purpose of this passage is to&rdquo; and &ldquo;The best title for this selection would be&rdquo; with responses in a multiple-choice format. The questions asked will be regarding the reading passages, such as the purpose of the passage, details about the text&rsquo;s key events or characters and your overall interest in each passage. There will be no questions that could link your identity to your responses on the test.&nbsp; <\/u><\/u><\/u>\n\n<div><u><u><u><strong>Risks\/Benefits\/Compensation&nbsp;<\/strong><\/u><\/u><\/u><\/div>\n<u><u><u> <u> There are no anticipated significant risks, benefits, or compensation for completing this study. <strong>Anonymity&nbsp;<\/strong> <u> Your responses will be strictly anonymous; we will not be collecting or retaining any information about your identity. The findings will be presented at the 2020 Western Psychological Association Convention in San Francisco. The SPSS and Excel files of the participants&rsquo; anonymous data will be archived indefinitely on the researchers&rsquo; password protected laptops and will be uploaded onto the project&rsquo;s Open Science Framework (OSF) page. OSF is a website dedicated to promoting research and facilitating collaboration.&nbsp; <strong>Right to Refuse or Withdraw<\/strong> <u> The decision to participate in this study is entirely up to you. &nbsp;You may refuse to take part in the study at any time without affecting your relationship with the investigators of this study or Pacific Lutheran University. &nbsp;Your decision to refuse will not result in any loss of benefits to which you are otherwise entitled. You have the right not to answer any single question, as well as to withdraw completely from the study at any point during the process. Because your participation is anonymous, it will not be possible to withdraw your survey answers from the study after you have submitted the survey.&nbsp; <strong>Right to Ask Questions and Report Concerns<\/strong> <u> You have the right to ask questions about this research and to have those questions answered by the researchers, before, during, or after the study. You may contact the primary investigators, Alexis Herion, at herionaw@plu.edu, and Cammy Widman, at widmancm@plu.edu, or the primary investigators&rsquo; faculty advisor Heidi McLaughlin at mclaughlinh@plu.edu. If you have any other concerns about your rights as a research participant, you may contact the Human Participants Review Board, Pacific Lutheran University through the Provost&rsquo;s Office at (253) 535-7126. <strong>Consent<\/strong> <u> By clicking below to be taken to the survey, you indicate that you have read and understood the above, that you are at least 18 years of age, that you willingly agree to participate, and that you are not waiving any legal claims. &nbsp; If you would like to keep a copy of this document for your records, please save this page now. <\/u><\/u><\/u><\/u><\/u><\/u><\/u><\/u>\n\n<div><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>&nbsp;<\/u><\/u><\/u><\/u><\/u><\/u><\/u><\/u><\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q1","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Consent to Participate in a Research Study Pacific Lutheran University Title of Study: The effect...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Take the Survey"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":2,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID766"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID767","SecondaryAttribute":"Consent to Participate in a Research Study Pacific Lutheran University Title of Study: The effect...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Consent to Participate in a Research Study<br \/>\nPacific Lutheran University<\/strong><\/div>\n\n<div><br \/>\n<strong>Title of Study:<\/strong> The effect of mind wandering and text difficulty on reading comprehension: A replication study.&nbsp;<br \/>\n<strong>Investigators: <\/strong>&nbsp;Alexis Herion and Cammy Widman, senior undergraduate students&nbsp;<br \/>\n<strong>Introduction<\/strong><\/div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>You are being asked to be in a research study conducted at Pacific Lutheran University in Psychology.<\/li>\n\t<li>You were selected to participate because you are at least 18 years old AND:&nbsp;\n\t<ul>\n\t\t<li>You are a PLU student with a SONA-systems account OR<\/li>\n\t\t<li>You were recruited via social media<\/li>\n\t<\/ul>\n\t<\/li>\n\t<li>The purpose of the study is to see the effect mind wandering and text difficulty has on reading comprehension. The purpose of this is to try to see the level of cognitive difficulty that results in more mind wandering. Also, to see if interest level affects mind wandering and reading comprehension.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<div><strong>Description of the Study Procedures<\/strong><\/div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>If you agree to be in this study, you will be asked to do the following things: Take a reading comprehension test on a computer or smartphone, which consists of eight passages for you to read and answer the corresponding questions at the end of each passage. As you read, you will be interrupted periodically with a question that asks if you were mind wandering while you read the previous sentence. After you finish reading all the passages and answering the corresponding reading comprehension questions, you will rate how interested you were in each passage that you previously read. The test should take you about 15 to 30 minutes.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t<li>Some sample questions we will ask are: &ldquo;The purpose of this passage is to&rdquo; and &ldquo;The best title for this selection would be&rdquo; with responses in a multiple-choice format. The questions asked will be regarding the reading passages, such as the purpose of the passage, details about the text&rsquo;s key events or characters and your overall interest in each passage. There will be no questions that could link your identity to your responses on the test.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<div><strong>Risks\/Benefits\/Compensation&nbsp;<\/strong><\/div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>There are no anticipated significant risks, benefits, or compensation for completing this study.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<strong>Anonymity&nbsp;<\/strong>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Your responses will be strictly anonymous; we will not be collecting or retaining any information about your identity. The findings will be presented at the 2020 Western Psychological Association Convention in San Francisco. The SPSS and Excel files of the participants&rsquo; anonymous data will be archived indefinitely on the researchers&rsquo; password protected laptops and will be uploaded onto the project&rsquo;s Open Science Framework (OSF) page. OSF is a website dedicated to promoting research and facilitating collaboration.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<strong>Right to Refuse or Withdraw<\/strong>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>The decision to participate in this study is entirely up to you. &nbsp;You may refuse to take part in the study at any time without affecting your relationship with the investigators of this study or Pacific Lutheran University. &nbsp;Your decision to refuse will not result in any loss of benefits to which you are otherwise entitled. You have the right not to answer any single question, as well as to withdraw completely from the study at any point during the process. Because your participation is anonymous, it will not be possible to withdraw your survey answers from the study after you have submitted the survey.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<strong>Right to Ask Questions and Report Concerns<\/strong>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>You have the right to ask questions about this research and to have those questions answered by the researchers, before, during, or after the study. You may contact the primary investigators, Alexis Herion, at herionaw@plu.edu, and Cammy Widman, at widmancm@plu.edu, or the primary investigators&rsquo; faculty advisor Heidi McLaughlin at mclaughlinh@plu.edu.<\/li>\n\t<li>If you have any other concerns about your rights as a research participant, you may contact the Human Participants Review Board, Pacific Lutheran University through the Provost&rsquo;s Office at (253) 535-7126.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<strong>Consent<\/strong>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>By clicking below to be taken to the survey, you indicate that you have read and understood the above, that you are at least 18 years of age, that you willingly agree to participate, and that you are not waiving any legal claims. &nbsp;<\/li>\n\t<li>If you would like to keep a copy of this document for your records, please save this page now.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q1","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Consent to Participate in a Research Study Pacific Lutheran University Title of Study: The effect...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Take the Survey"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":2,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID767"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID378","SecondaryAttribute":"Curiously enough, another important artist of about the same time was scorned even by many of his...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Curiously enough, another important artist of about the same time was scorned even by many of his own contemporaries.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Curiously enough, another important artist of about the same time was scorned even by many of his...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Curiously, about the same time, another important artist was scorned even by many of his contemporaries.","DataExportTag":"Q378","QuestionID":"QID378","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID191","SecondaryAttribute":"Curiously, about the same time, another important artist was scorned even by many of his contempo...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Curiously, about the same time, another important artist was scorned even by many of his contemporaries.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q191","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Curiously, about the same time, another important artist was scorned even by many of his contempo...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID191"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID39","SecondaryAttribute":"Daytimes Browning walked forth with Elizabeth's little dog Flush, but he seldom could be lured fr...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Daytimes Browning walked forth with Elizabeth's little dog Flush, but he seldom could be lured from his home evenings.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q39","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Daytimes Browning walked forth with Elizabeth's little dog Flush, but he seldom could be lured fr...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID39"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID255","SecondaryAttribute":"Daytimes Browning walked forth with Elizabeth's little dog Flush, but he seldom could be lured fr...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Daytimes Browning walked forth with Elizabeth's little dog Flush, but he seldom could be lured from his home evenings.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Daytimes Browning walked forth with Elizabeth's little dog Flush, but he seldom could be lured fr...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Daytimes Browning walked forth with Elizabeth's little dog Flush, but he seldom could be lured from his home evenings.","DataExportTag":"Q255","QuestionID":"QID255"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID763","SecondaryAttribute":"Debriefing\u00a0 Pacific Lutheran University \u00a0 Title of Study: The effect of mind wandering and text d.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Debriefing&nbsp;<\/strong><\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Pacific Lutheran University<\/strong><\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div><strong>Title of Study: <\/strong>The effect of mind wandering and text difficulty on reading comprehension: A replication study.&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div><strong>Investigator(s):<\/strong><\/div>\n\n<div>Alexis Herion, Psychology Department, herionaw@plu.edu<\/div>\n\n<div>Cammy Widman, Psychology Department, widmancm@plu.edu<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div><strong>Faculty Supervisor:&nbsp;<\/strong><\/div>\n\n<div>Heidi McLaughlin, Psychology Department, mclaughlinh@plu.edu<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>Thank you for your participation in our research study.&nbsp; The purpose of the study is to test the effect of mind wandering and text difficulty on reading comprehension.&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>We were interested in the topic because past research has shown that mind wandering has influenced areas such as reading comprehension. We expanded on that by doing a replication study that measured mind wandering and reading comprehension while manipulating the variable of text difficulty. We wanted to know if the results of the previous study would be consistent at PLU. We also added the variable of interest in the reading passages to test whether or not interest affects the amount of mind wandering.&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>We hypothesized that mind wandering would increase while reading the difficult texts, thus causing a decrease in reading comprehension.<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>The findings of this study will be presented at the 2020 Western Psychological Association Convention in San Francisco.<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>If you have any questions or concerns please feel free to contact one of us, or our faculty supervisor at the email listed at the top.&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>If you have any questions or concerns about this study or your rights as a study participant, you may contact the Human Participants Review Board, Pacific Lutheran University through the Provost&rsquo;s Office at (253) 535-7126.&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>Please do not discuss this study with other potential participants until the semester is over. If people know what we are testing before the study begins, they may respond differently, jeopardizing our results.&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>Thank you again for your help!<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q738","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Debriefing\u00a0 Pacific Lutheran University \u00a0 Title of Study: The effect of mind wandering and text d...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID763"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"RS","PrimaryAttribute":"RS_8HQZLHUAUV92xRH","SecondaryAttribute":"Default Response Set","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":null},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID394","SecondaryAttribute":"Differences among individual subjects cannot systematically confound the results if assignment to...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Differences among individual subjects cannot systematically confound the results if assignment to conditions is truly random.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Differences among individual subjects cannot systematically confound the results if assignment to...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"In the latter case, if assignment to conditions is truly random then prevailing differences among individual subjects cannot confound the results systematically.","DataExportTag":"Q394","QuestionID":"QID394","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID260","SecondaryAttribute":"During the third year of their stay in Italy, a son, Robert Weidemann Browning, was born.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"During the third year of their stay in Italy, a son, Robert Weidemann Browning, was born.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"During the third year of their stay in Italy, a son, Robert Weidemann Browning, was born.","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"The Brownings had a son, Robert Weidemann Browning, during the third year of their stay in Italy.","DataExportTag":"Q260","QuestionID":"QID260","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID24","SecondaryAttribute":"Elizabeth Barrett Browning was a pure singer with a lovely lyrical tenderness.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Elizabeth Barrett Browning was a pure singer with a lovely lyrical tenderness.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q24","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Elizabeth Barrett Browning was a pure singer with a lovely lyrical tenderness.","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID24"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID9","SecondaryAttribute":"Elizabeth Barrett was wise enough to see that Browning was a fine poet.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Elizabeth Barrett was wise enough to see that Browning was a fine poet.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q9","QuestionID":"QID9","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Elizabeth Barrett was wise enough to see that Browning was a fine poet.","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":24,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID46","SecondaryAttribute":"Elizabeth Browning\u2019s father died still disapproving of her marriage.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Elizabeth Browning\u2019s father died still disapproving of her marriage.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q46","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Elizabeth Browning\u2019s father died still disapproving of her marriage.","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID46"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID262","SecondaryAttribute":"Elizabeth Browning\u2019s father died unrelenting in his disavowal of her marriage, refusing to see he.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Elizabeth Browning\u2019s father died unrelenting in his disavowal of her marriage, refusing to see her or to sanction any of his family to see her.&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Elizabeth Browning\u2019s father died unrelenting in his disavowal of her marriage, refusing to see he...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Elizabeth Browning\u2019s father died still disapproving of her marriage.","DataExportTag":"Q262","QuestionID":"QID262","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID49","SecondaryAttribute":"Elizabeth drooped and grieved a little and Robert shielded her from ordinary visitors.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Elizabeth drooped and grieved a little and Robert shielded her from ordinary visitors.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q49","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Elizabeth drooped and grieved a little and Robert shielded her from ordinary visitors.","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID49"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID48","SecondaryAttribute":"Elizabeth\u2019s dearly loved sister died and left three children who were all younger than her own bo.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Elizabeth\u2019s dearly loved sister died and left three children who were all younger than her own boy.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q48","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Elizabeth\u2019s dearly loved sister died and left three children who were all younger than her own bo...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID48"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID223","SecondaryAttribute":"End of Experiment The purpose of this experiment is to assess the effect of mind-wandering on rea...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"End of Experiment<div><br><\/div><div>The purpose of this experiment is to assess the effect of mind-wandering on reading difficulty. Some of the passages are difficult to comprehend and some are easy to comprehend. The hypothesis for this experiment is that you will mind-wander more while reading the hard passages relative to the easy passages. Your performance on the reading comprehension test will also go down as you mind-wander. Additionally, you should read relatively slower during the hard condition than the easy condition.<\/div><div><br><\/div><div>Thank You for Participating!<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q223","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"End of Experiment The purpose of this experiment is to assess the effect of mind-wandering on rea...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID223"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID107","SecondaryAttribute":"Even most skeptics, because they seem to share the hope that there is life on Mars, endeavor slav...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Even most skeptics, because they seem to share the hope that there is life on Mars, endeavor slavishly not to discount the possibility.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q107","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Even most skeptics, because they seem to share the hope that there is life on Mars, endeavor slav...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID107"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID298","SecondaryAttribute":"Every second, a million times as much energy as is stored in all our coal, petroleum, and natural...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Every second, a million times as much energy as is stored in all our coal, petroleum, and natural gas fields is sent into space by the sun.&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Every second, a million times as much energy as is stored in all our coal, petroleum, and natural...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Every second, the sun sends a million times more energy into space than we have stored in all of our coal, petroleum, and natural gas fields.","DataExportTag":"Q298","QuestionID":"QID298","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID95","SecondaryAttribute":"Every second, the sun sends a million times more energy into space than we have stored in all of...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Every second, the sun sends a million times more energy into space than we have stored in all of our coal, petroleum, and natural gas fields.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q95","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Every second, the sun sends a million times more energy into space than we have stored in all of...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID95"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID320","SecondaryAttribute":"Few people seemed to care about life on Mars by the time Viking I landed on the Plain of Chrise i...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Few people seemed to care about life on Mars by the time Viking I landed on the Plain of Chrise in August.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Few people seemed to care about life on Mars by the time Viking I landed on the Plain of Chrise i...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"By the time Viking I touched down on the Plain of Chryse in August, few seemed to care at all.&nbsp;","DataExportTag":"Q320","QuestionID":"QID320","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID131","SecondaryAttribute":"Fungi give cheese the flavor, odor, and character that gourmets so highly prize.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Fungi give cheese the flavor, odor, and character that gourmets so highly prize.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q131","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Fungi give cheese the flavor, odor, and character that gourmets so highly prize.","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID131"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID34","SecondaryAttribute":"Hawthorne saw the Browning's there: the New England thinker and essayist Margaret Fuller visited...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Hawthorne saw the Browning's there: the New England thinker and essayist Margaret Fuller visited them.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q34","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Hawthorne saw the Browning's there: the New England thinker and essayist Margaret Fuller visited...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID34"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID250","SecondaryAttribute":"Hawthorne saw the Browning's there: the New England thinker and essayist Margaret Fuller visited...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Hawthorne saw the Browning's there: the New England thinker and essayist Margaret Fuller visited them.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Hawthorne saw the Browning's there: the New England thinker and essayist Margaret Fuller visited...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Hawthorne saw the Browning's there: the New England thinker and essayist Margaret Fuller visited them.","DataExportTag":"Q250","QuestionID":"QID250"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID23","SecondaryAttribute":"He called her his \u201cmoon of poets,\u201d and she considered him her sun.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p>He called her his \u201cmoon of poets,\u201d and she considered him\nher sun.<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q23","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"He called her his \u201cmoon of poets,\u201d and she considered him her sun.","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID23"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_dcdYhRXVG6jPrDL","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID239","SecondaryAttribute":"He called her his \u201cmoon of poets,\u201d as she considered him her sun.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p>He called her his \u201cmoon of poets,\u201d as she considered him\nher sun.<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"He called her his \u201cmoon of poets,\u2